# Build-time configuration applied by `vite build --mode vercel`
# (see the build:vercel script in package.json).
#
# SPLIT DEPLOY: the API runs on a separate container host (Render/Railway/Fly),
# NOT on Vercel. So VITE_API_BASE must be the backend's ABSOLUTE URL. The client
# (src/api.ts) already handles a cross-origin base and prefixes it onto media
# URLs automatically.
#
# Two ways to set it, in precedence order:
#   1. A Vercel Project Environment Variable named VITE_API_BASE (recommended —
#      Vite picks it up at build and it overrides the value below). Set it in
#      Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables.
#   2. The value below, committed here as a fallback.
#
# Replace the placeholder with your deployed backend URL, e.g.
#   VITE_API_BASE=https://platevision-api.onrender.com
# It must match the backend's host. API_PREFIX is empty on the container deploy,
# so do NOT append /api here.
VITE_API_BASE=https://YOUR-BACKEND-HOST.onrender.com
